/*
  =====================================================================
  EV VEHICLE TRACKER - Prototype Firmware v4.0  (Local Wi-Fi Web Dashboard)
  GPS Tracking | Engine ON/OFF | Battery Removal Alarm | Immobiliser | SMS
  MCU     : ESP32 DevKit V1 (Board: "ESP32 Dev Module")
  Network : 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi (router / phone hotspot) + backup soft-AP "EV-Tracker"
  Alerts  : Live web dashboard (http://<IP> or http://evtracker.local)
            + SMS to the owner through the SIM800L (optional)
  No cloud and no Firebase in this version.
  =====================================================================

  PIN MAP (matches schematic EVT-SCH-03 - frozen)
    GPS  UART2   : GPIO16 (RX2) <- GPS TX,  GPIO17 (TX2) -> GPS RX
    SIM800L UART1: GPIO26 (RX1) <- SIM TXD, GPIO27 (TX1) -> 1k/3k3 divider -> SIM RXD
    SIM800L RST  : GPIO4  (open-drain: driven LOW to reset, otherwise input)
    Relay        : GPIO25
    Engine sense : GPIO34 (input only, EXTERNAL 10k pull-up to 3.3V)
    I2C INA226   : GPIO21 SDA, GPIO22 SCL  (INA226 powered from 3.3V)
    Buzzer       : GPIO13 -> 1k -> BC547 base
    Status LED   : GPIO2  (solid = Wi-Fi connected, blinking = not connected)

  LIBRARIES (Arduino Library Manager)
    1. TinyGPSPlus   by Mikal Hart
    2. TinyGSM       by Volodymyr Shymanskyy   (only when USE_SIM800L is true)
    3. INA226        by Rob Tillaart (v0.5.x or newer)
    Built in to the ESP32 core: WiFi, WebServer, ESPmDNS, Preferences, Wire
    Board package: esp32 by Espressif Systems 2.0.x (2.0.17 tested setup) or 3.x

  WEB PAGE
    The dashboard lives in web/index.html. After editing it run
        python tools/embed.py
    which regenerates web_index.h in this folder (gzip-compressed).
=====================================================================
*/

